---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="CV"
  description="Curriculum vitae of Robbe De Win: bioinformatics-trained and data-driven, MSc Bioinformatics and MSc Biomedical Sciences, KU Leuven."
>
  <div class="page-head cv-head">
    <div>
      <p class="prompt">cat cv.md</p>
      <h1>Curriculum vitae</h1>
      <p class="page-head__summary">Last updated October 2026.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/cv/Robbe_De_Win_CV.pdf" download>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
        stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4" />
        <polyline points="7 10 12 15 17 10" />
        <line x1="12" y1="15" x2="12" y2="3" />
      </svg>
      download pdf
    </a>
  </div>

  <section class="cv-section">
    <h2>profile</h2>
    <div class="cv-section__body">
      <p>
        Bioinformatics-trained and data-driven, with two completed master's degrees.
        I use data to make decisions and automate what shouldn't be manual: most
        recently an automated pipeline that builds and validates metabolic models for
        roughly 1,500 bacterial genomes, and outside research a reproducible financial
        planning engine and a cycling coach that adapts its own plan every day.
        Comfortable owning a pipeline end to end — ingestion, quality control,
        validation against real-world data, and the reproducibility discipline that
        makes results trustworthy. Python and R daily, Linux and Git as everyday tools.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cv-section">
    <h2>education</h2>
    <div class="cv-section__body">
      <div class="cv-entry">
        <div class="cv-entry__head">
          <span class="cv-entry__title">Master of Bioinformatics</span>
          <span class="cv-entry__when">2024 – 2026</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cv-entry__where">KU Leuven · Cum Laude</div>
        <ul>
          <li>Thesis: <em>Pan-Metabolic Modelling Software for Therapeutics</em></li>
          <li>
            Relevant coursework: Machine Learning, Artificial Neural Networks,
            Bayesian Modelling, Comparative &amp; Regulatory Genomics, Evolutionary
            and Quantitative Genetics
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="cv-entry">
        <div class="cv-entry__head">
          <span class="cv-entry__title">Master of Biomedical Sciences</span>
          <span class="cv-entry__when">2022 – 2024</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cv-entry__where">KU Leuven · Cum Laude</div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Thesis: <em>Genetic Changes and Allele-Specific Expression in Induction
            Failure T-Cell Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia</em>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="cv-entry">
        <div class="cv-entry__head">
          <span class="cv-entry__title">Bachelor of Biomedical Sciences</span>
          <span class="cv-entry__when">2019 – 2022</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cv-entry__where">KU Leuven · Magna Cum Laude</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cv-section">
    <h2>research</h2>
    <div class="cv-section__body">
      <div class="cv-entry">
        <div class="cv-entry__head">
          <span class="cv-entry__title">
            MSc thesis — Pan-Metabolic Modelling Software for Therapeutics
          </span>
          <span class="cv-entry__when">2025 – 2026</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cv-entry__where">KU Leuven</div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Built <code>PaRMMoSaHN</code>, an open-source Python package that
            reconstructs one pan-metabolic model per species (PPanGGOLiN pangenome
            searched with gapseq) and derives every strain model from it by DIAMOND
            protein-homology projection — minutes per genome instead of hours.
          </li>
          <li>
            Validated on 1,010 <em>Clostridia</em> and 481 <em>Bacillus subtilis</em>
            genomes plus seven in-house lab strains, scored against Biolog
            substrate-utilisation data as Matthews correlation coefficient.
          </li>
          <li>
            Matched or exceeded per-genome reconstruction by gapseq and CarveMe in
            every cohort, with the highest pooled MCC on eight held-out
            <em>B. subtilis</em> strains, at roughly 12× the throughput on the largest
            cohort.
          </li>
          <li>
            Model QC with memote; downstream flux balance analysis, gene essentiality
            and auxotrophy prediction.
          </li>
          <li>
            Code:
            <a href="https://github.com/robbedewin/PaRMMoSaHN" rel="noopener">
              github.com/robbedewin/PaRMMoSaHN
            </a>
            · <a href="/projects/parmmosahn">write-up</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="cv-entry">
        <div class="cv-entry__head">
          <span class="cv-entry__title">
            MSc thesis — Genetic Changes and Allele-Specific Expression in Induction
            Failure T-ALL
          </span>
          <span class="cv-entry__when">2023 – 2024</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cv-entry__where">KU Leuven</div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Built Snakemake WGS and RNA-seq pipelines on the telomere-to-telomere
            T2T-CHM13 reference to profile induction-failure T-ALL patient samples:
            somatic and structural variant calling (Mutect2, GRIDSS) and copy-number
            analysis (ASCAT).
          </li>
          <li>
            Implemented a beta-binomial test for allele-specific expression combining
            DNA-derived allele counts with RNA read counts. Recovered known
            <em>NOTCH1</em> and <em>CDKN2A/B</em> lesions and identified <em>FAT1</em>
            as showing strong allele-specific expression.
          </li>
          <li><a href="/projects/tall-allele-specific-expression">Write-up</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cv-section">
    <h2>skills</h2>
    <div class="cv-section__body">
      <dl class="cv-skills">
        <div>
          <dt>Languages</dt>
          <dd>Python, R, Bash; LaTeX</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Bioinformatics</dt>
          <dd>
            Genome-scale metabolic modelling (gapseq, CarveMe, memote), flux balance
            analysis, pangenome analysis (PPanGGOLiN, DIAMOND), gene essentiality and
            auxotrophy prediction; WGS/RNA-seq variant calling (Mutect2, GRIDSS,
            ASCAT), allele-specific expression
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Workflows</dt>
          <dd>Snakemake, conda, reproducible staged pipelines</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Data &amp; ML</dt>
          <dd>
            Machine learning and neural networks, Bayesian modelling,
            high-dimensional data analysis, statistical validation
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Engineering</dt>
          <dd>
            Git/GitHub, Linux, conda environment management, pytest, Quarto,
            reproducible pipeline design, long-running batch workloads
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cv-section">
    <h2>software</h2>
    <div class="cv-section__body">
      <div class="cv-entry">
        <div class="cv-entry__head">
          <span class="cv-entry__title">financial_report &amp; market_data</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            A Quarto-based financial planning report generator for Belgian households,
            fed by an instrument registry and price-series store with as-of time travel
            so reports reproduce exactly. Tested with pytest, CI on GitHub Actions.
            <a href="/projects/financial-planning-engine">Write-up</a> · private repositories
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="cv-entry">
        <div class="cv-entry__head">
          <span class="cv-entry__title">BikeVault</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            A local-first garage inventory in Markdown and YAML with a stdlib-only
            Python toolchain: CSV/SQLite export and per-component mileage derived from
            training-log data. <a href="/projects/bikevault">Write-up</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cv-section">
    <h2>work</h2>
    <div class="cv-section__body">
      <div class="cv-entry">
        <div class="cv-entry__head">
          <span class="cv-entry__title">Student summer job</span>
          <span class="cv-entry__when">2017 – 2025</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cv-entry__where">Belcar (automotive)</div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Nine consecutive summers with the same employer: vehicle handling and
            on-site movement, plus administrative support.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="cv-entry">
        <div class="cv-entry__head">
          <span class="cv-entry__title">Delivery driver (student)</span>
          <span class="cv-entry__when">2020 – 2022</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cv-entry__where">B.B. Trans</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cv-section">
    <h2>languages</h2>
    <div class="cv-section__body">
      <dl class="cv-skills">
        <div><dt>Dutch</dt><dd>Native</dd></div>
        <div><dt>English</dt><dd>Full professional proficiency</dd></div>
        <div><dt>French</dt><dd>Basic</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cv-section">
    <h2>contact</h2>
    <div class="cv-section__body">
      <p>
        <a href="mailto:robbedewin@hotmail.com">robbedewin@hotmail.com</a> ·
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/robbedewin" rel="noopener">linkedin.com/in/robbedewin</a> ·
        <a href="https://github.com/robbedewin" rel="noopener">github.com/robbedewin</a>
        <br />
        Leuven, Belgium.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
